  <descriptions>
    <description descriptionType="Abstract">Illustrative record (fictional study) showing how a dataset collected with the Climate Change Concept Inventory is described with the HuMeta profile, including its Education module.</description>
    <description descriptionType="Methods">Study design: Quasi-experimental; Pre/post measurement around an intervention. Research questions: How does students' understanding of basic climate change processes change over a semester of active-learning instruction? Sampling: Non-probability: availability / convenience (including volunteers). Data collection: Test or assessment; Survey or questionnaire. Analysis: Statistical or quantitative analysis; Psychometric or measurement modeling (e.g., factor analysis, IRT). Participants: Students enrolled in two sections of an introductory Earth science course.</description>
    <description descriptionType="Other">Ethics and access (HuMeta profile). Human participants: Yes: people take part directly (surveys, interviews, observation, tests, creative work). Human-subjects review: Exempt determination. Participation consent: Informed consent. Consent for data sharing: Broad sharing of de-identified data consented. Identifiability: De-identified. Access level: Open (public).</description>
    <description descriptionType="Other">CARE statement (HuMeta profile). Indigenous data: No. Governance: Not applicable.</description>
  </descriptions>
